{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program has no `model` block, no parameters, and no sampling statements; all top-level data variables are context inputs used for deterministic transformed-data and generated-quantities calculations, not protected observations.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  vector tail_condition(vector y, vector theta, array[] real x_r, array[] int x_i) {
    vector[2] diff;

    if (!is_nan(y[1]) && !is_nan(y[2])) {
      diff[1] = inv_gamma_cdf(theta[1] | exp(y[1]), exp(y[2])) - 0.01;
      diff[2] = inv_gamma_cdf(theta[2] | exp(y[1]), exp(y[2])) - 0.99;
    } else {
      diff[1] = 0;
      diff[2] = 0;
    }
    return diff;
  }
}

data {
  real theta_l;
  real theta_u;
  real delta;
}

transformed data {
  real alpha_guess = square(delta * (theta_l + theta_u) / (theta_u - theta_l)) + 2;
  real beta_guess =  (alpha_guess - 1) * 0.5 * (theta_l + theta_u);
  vector[2] y_guess = [log(alpha_guess), log(beta_guess)]';
  vector[2] theta = [theta_l, theta_u]';
  array[0] real x_r;
  array[0] int x_i;

  print("Guesses:");
  print("  alpha = ", alpha_guess);
  print("  beta = ", beta_guess);
}

generated quantities {
  real alpha;
  real beta;
  {
    vector[2] y = algebra_solver(tail_condition, y_guess, theta, x_r, x_i);
    alpha = exp(y[1]);
    beta = exp(y[2]);
  }
}
